      "If time allows, continue your visit to <strong>Mehtab Bagh</strong>, a charbagh complex offering stunning views of the <strong>Taj Mahal</strong> from across the Yamuna River. This tranquil garden is the perfect spot to capture the Taj’s beauty during sunset, as the changing hues of the sky create a magical backdrop.",
      "<strong>Dinner and overnight stay in Agra.</strong><h2><a id=\"_vxpb54g7q2mp\"></a><strong>Day 8: Agra Sightseeing, Return to Delhi, and Departure (Road: 230 km, 4-5 hours)</strong></h2>Wake early for a sunrise visit to the <strong>Taj Mahal (Closed on Friday)</strong>, a UNESCO World Heritage Site and breathtaking symbol of love, its white marble glowing in the morning light. Its symmetrical white marble, inlaid with semi-precious stones, and serene gardens make it a global architectural wonder.",
