          "Thereafter, visit the Tea Museum, established in 2005, showcasing the rich history of tea production. Explore vintage tea-processing machines, enjoy aromatic tastings, and learn how Munnar’s tea heritage turned leaves into the perfect brew—a treat for tea lovers and curious travelers alike.",
          "Next, head to Echo Point, a scenic spot surrounded by misty hills known for its natural echo phenomenon. Shout out your name, and the hills will call it back—making it a fun, memorable experience. In the afternoon, unwind with an optional Ayurveda spa session, offering a holistic approach to wellness through ancient healing techniques like Abhyanga (oil massage), Shirodhara (oil pouring on the forehead), Panchakarma (detoxification), and herbal steam baths to restore balance and promote relaxation.",
